{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/46","id":4686665259,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1jWKw","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/46","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/46.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/46.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/46","number":46,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Correct known real-periodic rational-map interior status (30004438)","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Correct the real-periodic rational-map interior status (30004438)\n\n## Existing result\n\nThe full nonempty-interior question was answered by Kozhasov–Kummer in arXiv:2004.10003v1, Theorem 2 (April 2020), and remains covered by the current v2. This package corrects the imported assessment that only lower-dimensional families were known. It claims no new discovery and does not claim a verified journal publication.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe original OWR Questions 1–2 and both preprint versions were checked. The known construction is spelled out in the full real projective coefficient chart, with an all-iterate argument. All 51 exact controls pass. No statement about the Hermite conjecture or higher-dimensional projective space is implied.\n\nSeparate source/mathematical review passed the exact frozen artifact with no mandatory correction. All 848 independent exact controls pass. The package is AI-reviewed and unrefereed. Shared queue changes belong to the coordinator; recommended status is already_solved with existing-author credit.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:19:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:21:51Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1cb70b7af59b9203a88c870f4e921c7b9b77468c","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/46/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/46/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/46/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-30004438","ref":"dot/math-30004438","sha":"a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscri